          Peer review is how science advances. Good reviewers are generous with stars and precise with wishes: rather than "fix your writing", say "specify that 30 university students were tested" or "use 'suggests' instead of 'proves'".
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========================================================================
         STEP 5: CASE FILE #3 (8 MIN · FINAL DOSSIER & VERDICT)
         ========================================================================= -->
    <section id="panel-5" class="game-panel hidden space-y-8">
      <div class="bg-white border border-navy/10 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm space-y-6">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-navy/10 pb-4">
          <div>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-blue font-semibold">Step 5 · 8 min · The Verdict</span>
            <h2 class="font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mt-1">Case File #3: Ready for Yacine</h2>
            <p class="text-body text-[14px] mt-1">
